        "node_id": "n_7_768a25",
        "thought_text": "The current reasoning step is flawed because it only checks if A and B are within the range 1-9, which is incorrect. Takahashi can multiply any two integers between 1 and 9 (inclusive), not just those within this range. The correct approach should be to check if both A and B are within the valid range of 1 to 9, and if so, perform the multiplication; otherwise, print -1.",
